{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":94276,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"f2c15ab5ed7eb1922186cb13f0918c95bf267bf2246cdcb323040346017ea580","packTokens":66278,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":905,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"contract-new","tokens":474,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"new-look","tokens":82,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"scaffold-rules","tokens":227,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"repomap","tokens":5,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"spec","tokens":37885,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"cb","tokens":1418,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"critic","tokens":4460,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"approved-design","tokens":16622,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"scaffold","tokens":3891,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":5,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"plan"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nYou plan the implementation of an approved spec in a TypeScript web app (React, with the factory's component kit; a new product starts from the scaffold of its approved design).\n- Give at least 2 options (one marked simplest), choose one, and write a decision record of at most 5 lines (adr).\n- Split into tasks TASK-1.. in dependency order. Each task: the requirements it delivers, fileScope (exact repo paths or narrow globs it may change, no overlap between tasks), 1-2 exemplar files to imitate, plannedLoc, approach (short instructions for the implementer).\n- Build in working slices, not layers. A criterion checked through the API or a screen passes only once that route or screen is wired, so the first task that adds a route or screen also wires the app's entry (the startup file, the router, the layout), and each later task adds its logic together with its own endpoint or screen. Code a slice needs (an entity, a helper) goes into the first slice that uses it, not into a task of its own. File scopes may not overlap, so have that first task register routes by convention (file-based routes, or every class of one kind found at startup): later tasks then add only their own files.\n- List a requirement on the task after which its criteria can pass. Do not leave the wiring to a last task that then holds every criterion checked through the app: each earlier task is then checked only there, in the longest and dearest task of the run. Only where the repo's structure forces layers, give the wiring task a dependsOn on every layer it serves.\n- dependsOn: only the tasks whose code this task really needs.\n- complexity, on every task: standard | rules-or-algorithm | external-dependency | compliance-sensitive | real-time | new-to-stack. Most tasks are standard. rules-or-algorithm is a task whose work is mostly business rules, validations, allowed state changes or calculations.\n- Test projects, test files and CI config are not in any file scope: tests are written separately.\n- stubs: for every NEW public type/method/endpoint the tests will call, give a compilable stub file (full file content) whose bodies throw new Error(\"not implemented\"), so tests compile before implementation. Existing APIs need no stubs. Stub paths must be inside a task's fileScope.\n- Outside systems (an email or SMS provider, a payment service, another company's API, a file store): the code reaches each one through one seam, a module of its own (one exported function per call it makes), and nothing else in the app calls the system directly. Use the seam the repo already has for that system; for a new one, give the seam as a stub, so the tests can put a stand-in behind it before the code exists. The system's settings (host, port, sender address, key) are read from configuration by name: put .env.example in the fileScope of the task that writes the seam's real implementation, and say in its approach that each new setting is declared there with an empty value.\n- protectedPathsDeclared: list any migration, CI, build-config or package-feed file you must change (a human will see it).\n- newDependencies: any npm package to add (name, version, registry). Prefer none.\n\nAPI CONTRACT. This product has a web app and an API in two repos, and both are built against one contract.\n- Give one more stub: path \"contracts/openapi.yaml\", content the full OpenAPI 3.0.3 document (YAML) of every operation the approved screens and requirements need. It is outside every task's fileScope: nobody implements it, both sides follow it.\n- Write it in block style, one key per line with two-space indents: no {...} or [...] on a line except an empty value (\"security: []\", \"{}\"). Put any text with an apostrophe, a colon or a # in double quotes. A file with whole operations on one line stops parsing at the first stray quote.\n- No YAML anchors, aliases or merge keys (&name, *name, <<): what is used twice is a schema, a response or a parameter under components, pointed at with $ref.\n- Every operation has an operationId (camelCase), its request body where it takes one, and every status code it answers with.\n- Schemas go under components/schemas with \"required\" lists. Take the field names and types from the approved screens' sample data; an id is an integer.\n- Every JSON response carries an \"example\" with believable data (the approved screens' sample rows): the web app's tests run against these examples.\n- The web app calls the API only through the client generated from this file (lib/api); do not plan a hand-written client, and put no path under lib/api in a stub or in a task's fileScope: the factory generates that folder.\n- What the spec lists as not changing with \"(API-SIDE)\" is behaviour the API side builds and tests: no task here builds it, and the contract still gives its operations and every status code they answer with.\n\nThe approved design is a new look: its implementers get design tokens (colours, type, corners, spacing as CSS variables). Put the app's global stylesheet or theme file in the fileScope of the first task that builds a screen, so the tokens are added once and the other screens use them.\n\nThe approved design is built in next-shadcn: before any task starts, the factory writes the component kit, the theme, the frame and navigation, and every approved page (its blocks, states, layers and text, with the approved sample data) into the repo. Those generated files are not in any task's scope.\n- TASK-1 is the design-system task: its fileScope is exactly the ui-scaffold's designSystemTask.fileScope (plus nothing else UI), and its approach is the designSystemTask.todo list.\n- Then one task per screen in ui-scaffold.screens: its fileScope includes that screen's container (and the API or service files the behaviour needs). The task gives the page real data, API calls, validation and the behaviour the requirements ask for, in the container; it does not restyle or rebuild the page.\n\nRepository map:\n","tools":["read_file","search","repo_map"],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"Departure is blocked until every expected route box is scanned and wrong-route boxes are removed or corrected.\",\n  \"Unsent work affected by an offline route change remains available for review and resolution; completed handovers are preserved.\",\n  \"An offline handover completed despite an On Hold conflict is retained, flagged, and associated with a quality case when synchronized.\",\n  \"Denied or unavailable browser location does not block a handover and is recorded as unavailable.\",\n  \"Live temperature, alert, box-association, and history data are supplied through an existing gateway API or feed.\",\n  \"A signer confirms identity using the sign-in method configured for that account.\",\n  \"Customer portal times use the user's configured account time zone.\",\n  \"Recall responses may leave a remainder unaccounted until later accounting or signed write-off.\",\n  \"Handover signatures and delivery photos are retained for seven years, matching audit-record retention.\",\n  \"A Quality Manager is authorized to sign a write-off.\",\n  \"Refusals are recorded by whole box, with a reason for each refused box.\",\n  \"One configured set of tier limits and allowances applies to all products.\",\n  \"Reports use on-screen date-range filters and CSV export; no custom report builder is included.\",\n  \"Quality-decision escalation and recall notices/reminders are email-only from fixed templates, with no SMS or push.\",\n  \"The customer portal and certificates support English and Arabic, including right-to-left Arabic layout.\",\n  \"The existing logger/gateway data and API/feed are supplied for consumption by the web app.\"\n ],\n \"critic\": [\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"REQ-21 lists ASM-18 as a source, which keeps gap-affected stock On Hold until resolved, but the same requirement (per Q-11/ASM-2) says the screen must not infer On Hold from a gap; the sources contradict each other and nothing settles which wins.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-21\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"REQ-24 and REQ-3 cite ASM-1 and ASM-17 ('No; online only'), yet REQ-24 queues offline driver actions and later syncs them under Q-10, so the sources state opposite rules for queued actions.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-24\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-6.1 and AC-6.3 show API-recalculated 'decision values' after a profile change, but no criterion requires that a changed not-permitted-range disposition goes back through the Quality Officer proposal and different-Quality-Manager approval required by Q-1/REQ-9.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Staff sign-in through 'Meridian Microsoft accounts' and a customer one-time-code step are not in any intent span or human answer (ASM-23's answer only states email, password and a reset link), so the identity provider and the second factor are unanchored.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-2.1 names the 'Meridian Microsoft' sign-in option directly instead of treating the staff identity provider or tenant as configuration.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"rubric\": 8,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-2.2 covers only the code-entry screen and has no criterion for a wrong, expired or repeatedly failed one-time code, or for a resend.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-14.3 says the screen 'shows only returned eligible dates' and also that it 'applies the next-working-day rule' for before and after cut-off, so it is unclear whether the browser computes eligibility or only displays what the API returns.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-14\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"'The workday ends' triggers clearing of cached route and recipient data in REQ-24, AC-24.7 and AC-24.8, but nothing defines when a workday ends or in which time zone (driver device or serving warehouse per ASM-6).\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-24\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"In AC-24.4 the action is shown 'as rejected or no longer queued', and the EARS says queued actions are 'erased or marked rejected', so the expected end state has two acceptable outcomes and cannot be checked deterministically.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-24\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-9.4 accepts either 'shows the returned error message or disables the approval control', so a test cannot tell which behaviour is required when the proposer tries to approve their own disposition.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"No criterion covers empty states (no temperature readings, no stock rows, a filter with no matches, no alerts), even though lists and histories appear throughout REQ-3, REQ-10, REQ-19, REQ-20 and REQ-27.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-19\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Several write flows have only a success criterion, with no API-refusal or network-failure path: stock movement (AC-12.1), address changes (AC-13.1), box sealing (AC-17.3) and route creation (AC-18.1).\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-10.1 asserts that the returned status quantities sum to on-hand but does not say what the screen shows if the API returns figures that do not reconcile.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-15.6 lets a Dispatcher cancel a Packed-or-later order, but no criterion says what the screen shows for the already packed box, its logger, or its place on a route after the cancellation.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-15\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-26.6 allows a recall to be closed without saying whether closing is allowed, blocked or warned while AC-26.4's unreconciled quantities are still outstanding.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-26\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-5.5 deactivates a product without covering what open orders, allocations or profile versions referencing it show afterwards, and the 'today' in AC-5.6 has no defined time zone.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"I-7 asks for role and warehouse access controls, but no requirement gives System Administrators a screen to assign staff roles or warehouses, or to disable accounts; only Customer Administrator invite and remove exists (REQ-4).\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-3.2 grants Quality Managers and Auditors all-warehouse views, but this scope is not anchored in any intent span or human answer.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-3.3 requires an 'API-refused write' to be shown as an error on Auditor pages that, by the same criterion, have no create, edit or delete controls, so that error path cannot be reached through the UI.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"To reconcile ASM-9 with ASM-21, REQ-8 adds a separate 'receipt-evidence' image/PDF upload that no intent span or answer asks for.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"rubric\": 4,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-8.1 relies on a 'configured supplier interface format' whose documentation, per ASM-8, Meridian has not yet provided, so no client-side validation of the logger file can be specified or tested.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"REQ-22 repeats REQ-21's gap behaviour (status and budget shown without an estimated tier charge), and its stability is 0.33, so the two requirements overlap and could drift apart.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-22\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"NFR-4 states volumes (1,000 users, 100,000 records, 5,000 devices) but sets no observable web-side target such as list or chart load time or pagination behaviour at that volume.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"NFR-4\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-27.1 says the CSV contains 'the displayed or filtered records', which leaves open whether it holds the current page or the full filtered set, and no criterion covers which roles may export records containing recipient names.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-27\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"REQ-15 cites Q-6 (addresses and shelf life) as a source for the order change and cancellation rules, and REQ-26 cites Q-1 for recalls; neither source supports the requirement it is attached to.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-15\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"No criterion covers the default language, whether the language choice persists across sessions, or how left-to-right identifiers such as lot codes and numbers render inside right-to-left Arabic pages.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-28\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"NFR-4 starts the 60-second trace budget when the response arrives, while NFR-5 starts it when the user makes the request, so the two give different pass conditions for the same lot-trace display.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"NFR-4\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"NFR-4 comes from Q-40's 'assumed launch scale', and REQ-22 cites ASM-7 (1,000 users / 100,000 records), but Q-16 rejected adding any scale target.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"NFR-4\",\n   \"rubric\": 4,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-16.1 picks the single-person controls when an eligible Quality Officer 'opens the decision form' based on whether 'the proposed decision matches the recommendation', but the decision is not proposed until the officer is inside that form, which clashes with AC-16.4 ('when a user prepares the decision').\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-44\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-16.4 also requires a two-person proposal and a different Quality Manager's approval when a decision opposes the recommendation, but the request (Q-26) lets a Quality Officer decide alone inside tier 1 with allowance left and only asks for a written justification on an opposing decision.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-44\",\n   \"rubric\": 4,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"There is no path for a Quality Manager declining or returning a Quality Officer's proposal, and no state for a declined proposal, so a two-person decision can only end in approval.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-44\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-17.1 requires identity confirmation at signing but has no criterion for a failed confirmation (wrong password) or an expired session, for example that nothing is shown as signed and the reason entered is kept.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-45\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-18.2 adds a rule that a superseding disposition is rejected after the stock was delivered or destroyed; no answer contains this rule, and ASM-1 says the superseding decision is applied to the stock and its order/route state.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-46\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The destruction quantity is checked only against 'the displayed rejected quantity', so several destruction entries for the same rejected stock can each pass and together exceed it; the requirement does not say the check uses the quantity still undestroyed.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-47\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Destruction entry has no role or access-denied criterion and does not say who may record destruction or witness it, unlike the other staff screens.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-47\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-24.3 expects 'a validation error or returned error message' and also 'sends no invalid response request', which cannot both hold: a returned error requires the request to have been sent.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-52\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-24.4 lets a customer revise quantities but does not say what happens after the unaccounted remainder has been written off or the recall has been closed.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-52\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The write-off has no criterion for a non-Quality-Manager user (Q-6 limits it to a Quality Manager), and does not say whether the 'signed justification' requires the identity re-confirmation used in REQ-17.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-53\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-21.1 and AC-21.2 require a 'signature' on recall start and close without saying what that signature is (identity re-confirmation as in REQ-17, or something else), and AC-21.3's 'not identified as eligible' names no role.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-49\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Handover has no validation path for a missing receiver name, signature or photo, and none for camera permission being denied or the photo capture failing.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-37\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"No criterion stops a refusal from being submitted when a refused box has no reason, although the requirement makes a reason mandatory for each refused box.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-39\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Departure is blocked until wrong boxes are 'removed or corrected', but no criterion defines how the driver un-scans, removes or corrects a wrong-route box to clear the block.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-32\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"There is no empty state for a driver with no routes today, and no criterion that today's route and expected boxes stay available offline, which REQ-12's offline loading and handover depend on.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-31\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The spec requires 'resolution' of affected unsent work but never lists the ways it can be resolved (discard, reassign, keep), and only covers route differences when unsent work exists, although the requirement says differences are always shown.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-41\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"There is no criterion for the gateway feed being unavailable or returning no data while the browser is online, and no rule for how old data must be before it counts as stale beyond 'disconnected'.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-34\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Account management does not say how a newly created account gets its first password (invite or set-password link), and has no validation criteria such as a duplicate email.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-30\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Deactivating an account does not say what happens to that user's active sessions, routes assigned to a deactivated driver, or that driver's offline queued work.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-30\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The spec relies on roles (Driver, Dispatcher, Quality Officer, Quality Manager, Auditor, System Administrator, customer) that REQ-2 assigns but never lists or defines, so the permission checks in REQ-30 and REQ-31 rest on undefined role names.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-30\",\n   \"rubric\": 8,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Dispatcher route monitoring, recall trace (REQ-22) and waiting decisions (REQ-20) have no access-denied criterion, while the other staff screens do.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-33\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-15.2 refers to users viewing tier-limit 'settings', but no requirement provides a screen to view or configure the single set of tier limits and allowances from Q-8, or says who may change it.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-43\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"There is no criterion for an account with no configured time zone, for where the user chooses English or Arabic, or for which time zone staff and driver screens use.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-57\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Opening-inventory entry is not limited to launch and has no rule against duplicate lots, so after go-live it stays a way to create stock outside receiving, which affects lot history and recall totals.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-61\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Customer order views have no empty state for an organisation with no orders, and AC-26.1 assumes one organisation per customer although Q-2 lets an administrator assign customer-organisation access without limiting it to one.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-54\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The 60-minute on-time window and the 60-day expiry horizon are fixed in the report definitions rather than set as configuration, as is the four-hour escalation threshold in REQ-20.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-60\",\n   \"rubric\": 8,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"REQ-3, REQ-5 and REQ-12 cite ASM-5 (fixed browser versions), and REQ-29 cites ASM-6 and ASM-18 (WCAG 2.1 AA), but the human rejected those assumptions in Q-14 and Q-15, so these sources are wrong.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-31\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  }\n ],\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-12T20:07:30.851Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"spec\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"stage\": \"specify\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261012-meridian-coldchain-platform-in-9fcb\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"lint\": [\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L1 ids\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L2 req-ac\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L3 ears\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L4 vague\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L5 nfr\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L6 scope\",\n   \"details\": \"out-of-scope list is empty; say explicitly what isn't changing\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L8 anchors\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L9 size\",\n   \"details\": \"This spec has 28 requirements, about 4 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L10 trace\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L11 observable\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L12 literals\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n   \"metric\": \"At viewport widths 320, 768, and 1280/1440 CSS pixels, zero horizontal overflow; phone interactive targets are at least 44 × 44 CSS pixels.\",\n   \"text\": \"Every portal page reflows for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow layouts.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n   \"metric\": \"100% of the agreed main-flow screens pass WCAG 2.1 AA checks; zero unmet applicable success criteria in audited main flows.\",\n   \"text\": \"Main staff, customer, and driver web flows conform to WCAG 2.1 Level AA.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n   \"metric\": \"100% of agreed main-flow UI test cases pass on the latest two versions of each of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n   \"text\": \"The responsive portals support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n   \"metric\": \"1,000 users, 100,000 records in the first year, and data from 5,000 devices reporting at once.\",\n   \"text\": \"The web portal supports the stated first-year user and record volume and displays data from the stated simultaneous device volume.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n   \"metric\": \"All pages render without horizontal scrolling at widths from 320 px through 1920 px; interactive touch targets on narrow viewports are at least 44 by 44 CSS px.\",\n   \"text\": \"The Meridian web app shall be responsive on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n   \"metric\": \"For every recall-trace response received, 100% of returned trace entries are displayed or accessible within 60 seconds after the response is received.\",\n   \"text\": \"The web app shall render the full recall trace returned by the service within 60 seconds after response receipt.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n   \"metric\": \"For 100% of lot-trace requests, the screen displays or makes accessible all returned trace entries within 60 seconds of the user's request; no user-count or record-volume target applies.\",\n   \"text\": \"The web client shall make the complete returned lot trace available through its screen within 60 seconds of the user's request.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"API-side enforcement of credentials, password-reset token validity/delivery, role and access-scope authorization, and account state; web requirements cover forms, requests, screens, and API response handling.\",\n  \"API-side persistence and enforcement of stock/order/route transitions, hold and recall blocking across warehouses, quarantine, quantity validation/conservation, recall trace completeness and arithmetic, recall closure eligibility, write-off authorization, and duplicate-handover idempotency.\",\n  \"API-side audit creation, tamper detection, immutability, seven-year retention of audit records and handover evidence, and certificate-version persistence.\",\n  \"API-side scheduled and outbound emails, including recall notices and 24-hour reminders, four-hour decision escalation, daily summaries, monthly reports, and monthly report generation; web screens display supplied results/status where specified.\",\n  \"API-side production of recall traces within a time limit; the client timing requirements measure rendering after the response or from the user's request, as specified in separate requirements.\",\n  \"Supplying live temperature readings, alerts, box associations, and history through the existing logger or supplier gateway feed.\",\n  \"Importing or guaranteeing initial database contents; the web app provides opening-lot and stock entry.\",\n  \"Pricing, invoicing and payments; route stop-order optimization; manufacturer purchasing and demand forecasting; automatic driver or customer penalties; stock transfers between warehouses; logger hardware and supplier gateway implementation.\",\n  \"Native iOS or Android applications, app-store distribution, push notifications, and background location. The product is a responsive web app; applicable notices use in-app notices or email, location uses the browser prompt, and the web app may be installable.\",\n  \"Offline-cache recall blocking and a separate quality-case flow for offline handovers that conflict with recall status (Q-11).\",\n  \"Account isolation for browser-local queued work and a user-review workflow for permanently rejected queued payloads (Q-13).\"\n ],\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A signed-in staff or customer user has portal access\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows links to the modules permitted for that user, including applicable stock, order, delivery, temperature, quality, and recall pages\",\n     \"when\": \"the user opens portal navigation\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A user opens an available workflow at phone, tablet, and desktop viewport widths\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen content has no horizontal overflow and phone controls have touch targets of at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels\",\n     \"when\": \"the page is rendered\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide role-oriented portal pages and navigation for stock, orders, deliveries, temperature monitoring, quality decisions, and recalls on phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"I-15\",\n    \"ASM-13\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A staff user opens staff sign-in\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the Meridian Microsoft sign-in option and no external staff-account form\",\n     \"when\": \"the user selects the staff sign-in flow\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns a one-time-code challenge after a customer submits email and password\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows a code-entry field, no customer social sign-in or single-sign-on option, and no customer account content before a successful code response\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer submits the credentials\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer user requests a password reset\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request contains the customer email address and the screen shows the reset-link-by-email confirmation returned by the API\",\n     \"when\": \"the reset request is submitted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A disabled or removed account attempts online sign-in or access\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows an access-denied message and no protected page or record is displayed\",\n     \"when\": \"the API returns an access-denied response\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide staff authentication through Meridian Microsoft accounts and customer authentication using email and password followed by a one-time code, with reset links requested by email and no social sign-in or single-sign-on option for customer accounts.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"ASM-23\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns records for a staff member's assigned warehouses or a customer's organisation\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows only the returned records\",\n     \"when\": \"the user opens the corresponding list\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Quality Manager or Auditor opens a warehouse-scoped list and the API returns all-warehouse records\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned records from all warehouses\",\n     \"when\": \"the list is displayed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An Auditor opens a record page\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows record details without create, edit, or delete controls, and an API-refused write is shown as an error message\",\n     \"when\": \"the page renders\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A protected request is refused because the account or record is inaccessible\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows an access-ended or access-denied message and clears protected record fields\",\n     \"when\": \"the web app receives the refusal\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a user opens portal views, the Meridian responsive web app shall show records and actions returned for that user's role, assigned warehouses, and customer organisation, present Auditor views as read-only, and clear protected data when the API refuses access.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"ASM-1\",\n    \"ASM-17\",\n    \"ASM-11\",\n    \"ASM-23\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator opens user management for their organisation\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the invitation or removal status returned by the API\",\n     \"when\": \"the administrator submits an invitation or removal\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API refuses a user-management action, including an action for another organisation\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned error message and does not show the other organisation's user as changed\",\n     \"when\": \"the administrator submits the action\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let a Customer Administrator invite and remove users through controls scoped to that administrator's customer organisation.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-7\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator searches by product name or code or opens a deactivated product\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows matching product records and identifies deactivated products as unavailable for ordering\",\n     \"when\": \"the API returns matching products and active states\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator submits an incomplete profile or one with overlapping or gapped tiers\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the validation error returned by the API and does not show the product as saved\",\n     \"when\": \"the administrator attempts to save\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator submits a valid profile with tiers, reason, and effective date\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request includes the profile tiers, reason, and effective date and the screen shows the new profile version returned by the API\",\n     \"when\": \"the profile change is submitted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A product has multiple profile versions\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen lists earlier versions with their returned values, reason, effective date, and creator where returned, and provides no edit controls for earlier versions\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens profile history\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator deactivates a product\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.5\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the product as deactivated\",\n     \"when\": \"the API returns the updated product status\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator enters a profile effective date before today\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.6\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows a validation error and no profile-save request is sent\",\n     \"when\": \"the administrator attempts to save the profile\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let System Administrators list, search, view, deactivate, and maintain products and create versioned temperature profiles with storage bands, contiguous non-overlapping tiers, allowance or not-permitted designations, a reason, and an effective date no earlier than today, while keeping earlier versions read-only.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"I-10\",\n    \"ASM-4\",\n    \"Q-12\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns a new effective profile version and recalculated values for stock still held from the effective date onward\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the new version's effective date and the returned budget and decision values\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens the profile and affected stock views\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A profile version has an effective date of today or later and the API returns an earlier quality decision for affected stock\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the earlier decision's returned values and status unchanged and does not show a recalculated earlier decision\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens the profile and affected stock views\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator submits a profile change with a reason and effective date\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the new version, reason, effective date, and returned recalculated budget and decision values\",\n     \"when\": \"the API returns the updated profile and affected-stock results\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A profile version takes effect and the API returns recalculation results for allocated, packed, or routed stock still held from the effective date onward\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned allocation, box, and route statuses and any returned action-required message or handover restriction\",\n     \"when\": \"an authorized user opens or refreshes the affected order, box, or route\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a temperature-profile version takes effect, the Meridian responsive web app shall show the new version and API-returned recalculated budgets, decisions, and current statuses for stock still held from its effective date onward, show earlier quality decisions as unchanged, and show resulting order, box, and route statuses for affected allocated or packed stock.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-11\",\n    \"I-17\",\n    \"Q-8\",\n    \"Q-12\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator opens the receipt form\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows fields for product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, cold room, and shelf\",\n     \"when\": \"the form is displayed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API accepts a receipt with an inbound logger file\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the receipt record, Quarantined status, submitted receipt details, and returned inbound readings and budget use when available\",\n     \"when\": \"the operator submits the receipt\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API refuses a receipt with an expired lot date or missing required field\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned error message beside the relevant field and no saved receipt is displayed\",\n     \"when\": \"the operator submits the receipt\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a Warehouse Operator records a receipt, the Meridian responsive web app shall capture product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, and storage location and show returned quarantine status and inbound temperature information before a release decision.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"ASM-9\",\n    \"ASM-21\",\n    \"ASM-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator uploads an inbound logger file in the configured supplier interface format\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request includes the uploaded logger file and the screen shows the returned inbound readings and budget use before release controls\",\n     \"when\": \"the receipt is submitted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator uploads a logger file rejected by the API\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned file error message and no successful-upload indicator\",\n     \"when\": \"the upload response is displayed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An operator uploads a separate receipt-evidence image or PDF larger than 10 MB or a separate receipt-evidence file that is not an image or PDF\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows a validation error and no saved receipt is displayed\",\n     \"when\": \"the operator attempts to submit the receipt\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide inbound logger-file upload and display returned temperature history and budget use, validate separate image or PDF receipt-evidence files, and accept logger exports in the supplier's documented format.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"ASM-8\",\n    \"ASM-9\",\n    \"ASM-21\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A quarantined receipt is opened by a Quality Officer\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows returned receipt data, temperature-budget use, and release decision controls\",\n     \"when\": \"the receipt review page renders\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A receipt is within 30 days of expiry on arrival or the API refuses release\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the reason returned by the API and does not display the stock as released\",\n     \"when\": \"a Quality Officer opens or submits the release decision\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Quality Officer proposes a disposition for stock exposed to a not-permitted range\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request includes the proposed disposition and reason and the screen shows the proposal awaiting a different Quality Manager's approval\",\n     \"when\": \"the proposal is submitted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The proposing person attempts to approve, or a user without the Quality Manager role attempts approval\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned error message or disables the approval control and shows the decision as unapproved\",\n     \"when\": \"the approval is attempted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A different Quality Manager approves or rejects a pending disposition\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.5\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned decision, decision-maker, and decision status\",\n     \"when\": \"the API returns the final decision\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When quality staff review a receipt or excursion, the Meridian responsive web app shall present available release or disposition actions and show decision states returned by the API, including separate proposal and approval steps for not-permitted-range dispositions.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-14\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"ASM-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns on-hand and status quantities for a product, lot, and warehouse\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the on-hand total and each returned status quantity as a separate field or row, with the quantities summing to the on-hand count\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens the stock view\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns stock rows for multiple lots or warehouses\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows only rows matching the selected filter values\",\n     \"when\": \"a user filters the stock list\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show on-hand stock with mutually exclusive quantities for available, allocated, quarantined, On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, and Expired statuses, and show returned warehouse, lot, product, receipt, and location details.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-11\",\n    \"I-17\",\n    \"Q-7\",\n    \"ASM-3\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A received lot is divided into handling units with different temperature histories\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows separate rows or records with each unit's returned quantity, history, and budget values\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens the lot's handling-unit view\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When portions of received stock have different temperature histories, the Meridian responsive web app shall show them as separate handling units with their returned quantity, history, and tier-budget use and remaining.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-13\",\n    \"I-14\",\n    \"Q-5\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator moves stock between shelves or cold rooms\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request includes the source and destination and the screen shows the returned movement record with actor, time, and quantity fields\",\n     \"when\": \"the operator submits the move and opens its result\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide stock-movement forms and show the returned movement record with source and destination locations, quantity, actor, and time.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator opens address management\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the address list or status returned by the API\",\n     \"when\": \"the administrator adds, edits, or removes an address\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator changes minimum remaining shelf life for a customer organisation\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request includes the organisation-level value and the screen shows the saved value and response status returned by the API\",\n     \"when\": \"the change is submitted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer user or Dispatcher opens an order form\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the organisation's minimum remaining shelf-life value without a control to change it per order\",\n     \"when\": \"the form renders\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let Customer Administrators maintain their organisation's saved delivery addresses and let System Administrators set the organisation's minimum remaining shelf-life requirement, showing that value read-only to customer users and Dispatchers.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-10\",\n    \"I-11\",\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"ASM-5\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer user opens the order form\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen provides fields for at least one product line, a quantity of at least one pack per line, a saved address, requested delivery date, and partial-or-complete delivery preference\",\n     \"when\": \"the form is displayed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer enters a quantity below one pack or submits an order without a line\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows a field error and the request is not sent\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer submits the form\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns eligible delivery dates for the serving warehouse, based on its configured local time, cut-off, working days, and holidays\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows only returned eligible dates, applies the next-working-day rule for an order before cut-off and no-earlier-than-the-working-day-after-that rule for an order after cut-off, and identifies the warehouse time zone\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer opens the date selector before or after the configured cut-off\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer selects a deactivated product for an order\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows that the product cannot be ordered and provides no orderable quantity field\",\n     \"when\": \"the product status is returned\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer selects products, quantities, address, date, and fulfillment choice\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.5\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the complete order summary\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer reviews the order before submission\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let customer users create orders with one or more product lines, pack quantities, an organisation-saved delivery address, an eligible delivery date, and a choice between delivery of available quantities and complete delivery only.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-10\",\n    \"ASM-5\",\n    \"ASM-6\",\n    \"ASM-27\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns an order with line quantities and a status before Packed\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows each line's allocated and outstanding quantities and customer change and cancel controls\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer opens the order\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns an order status of Packed or later\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the current status and no customer change or cancel controls\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer opens the order\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A cancellation or change is refused or accepted by the API\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned error or cancellation response, current status, updated quantities, and stock availability count when returned\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer submits the action or refreshes the order\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer submits an order more than once or retries after a network interruption\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \