x type, logger identifier, delivery stop, products, lots, and quantities\",\n     \"when\": \"the form renders\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The operator selects stock, a box type, and logger and submits the packing action\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned compatibility result or error message and does not show an unsuccessful box as sealed\",\n     \"when\": \"the API returns compatibility results or refuses an incompatible band, box type, missing logger, or already-associated logger\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A box is ready to be sealed and sealing succeeds\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows exactly one logger requirement and the returned seal time, operator, contents, quantities, and logger\",\n     \"when\": \"the operator opens the box record\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let Warehouse Operators pack stock into shipper boxes by type, associate one logger with each box, and show compatibility, contents, and sealing details returned by the API.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-12\",\n    \"I-13\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Dispatcher creates a route\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen provides fields for one vehicle, one driver, route date, at least one ordered stop, and planned arrival times\",\n     \"when\": \"the route form is displayed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API refuses confirmation because a box exceeds its qualified duration after applying the configured safety margin, which defaults to 4 hours\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the refused status, affected box, returned overage amount, and returned configured safety-margin value\",\n     \"when\": \"the Dispatcher views the result\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A confirmed route is changed before the driver has left for an affected stop\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request identifies the changed route and the screen shows returned stop order, schedule details, and driver notification status when returned\",\n     \"when\": \"the Dispatcher reorders or moves the stop\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A driver opens a changed confirmed route\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the changed stop or schedule details returned by the API\",\n     \"when\": \"the route view is displayed\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let Dispatchers create and view routes with a date, vehicle, driver, ordered stops, and planned arrival times and show route-confirmation errors and confirmed-route changes returned by the API, including configured qualified-duration safety margins.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-12\",\n    \"I-15\",\n    \"ASM-6\",\n    \"ASM-27\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns temperature history\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen provides chart and table views with readings positioned by event or reading time, band bounds, excursion markers, and visible gaps\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens the history page\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns duplicate, delayed, out-of-order, future-dated, pre-seal, or otherwise flagged readings\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows returned reading times and flags, identifies invalid-for-calculation readings, and displays returned history in time order without presenting excluded readings as calculation inputs\",\n     \"when\": \"the history is displayed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A user switches between chart and table views\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the corresponding returned history in each view\",\n     \"when\": \"the API returns the same history data\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns gateway batch readings or inbound logger-file reading results\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned readings and associated device or receipt\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens the relevant device or receipt history\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show temperature histories for boxes, cold rooms, and lots as charts and tables with returned readings, applicable bands, excursions, gaps, and reading flags or silence status.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"I-13\",\n    \"I-14\",\n    \"ASM-2\",\n    \"ASM-4\",\n    \"ASM-8\",\n    \"ASM-18\",\n    \"ASM-21\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns an excursion and its affected handling units\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows returned excursion start, end, readings, closure status, affected units, and used and remaining amounts by tier\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens excursion or budget details\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns an open excursion, handling units, and hold statuses\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows affected handling units, tier budgets, and returned hold statuses\",\n     \"when\": \"a Quality Officer opens the excursion view\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns a remaining-budget warning, exhausted tier, or not-permitted-range alert\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned alert category and affected stock or device\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens alerts or quality status\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns an alert for silence, excursion, low or exhausted budget, not-permitted range, or corrected excursion\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows returned alert type, affected device or stock, recipient role and delivery metadata when returned, plus corrected excursion or budget status when present\",\n     \"when\": \"an intended user opens alert history\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show excursions, handling-unit budget use and remaining allowances, returned alerts, and returned hold and decision statuses for affected devices and stock.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-20\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-13\",\n    \"I-14\",\n    \"I-15\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"Q-8\",\n    \"ASM-4\",\n    \"ASM-10\",\n    \"ASM-18\",\n    \"ASM-22\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns an unresolved temperature-history gap for affected stock, its review status, and its stock status\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-21.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the gap, review status, and returned stock status without estimating a temperature tier\",\n     \"when\": \"a Quality Officer opens the quality status\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns an unresolved gap flagged for review and a stock status of Available, with no other hold reason returned\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-21.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the Available status and review flag and does not show the stock as On Hold because of the gap\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens the affected stock detail\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When the API returns an unresolved temperature-history gap affecting stock, the Meridian responsive web app shall show the gap, review status, and stock status returned by the API without inferring an On Hold status from the gap or displaying an estimated temperature tier.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-21\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"I-13\",\n    \"I-14\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"Q-11\",\n    \"ASM-2\",\n    \"ASM-18\",\n    \"ASM-11\",\n    \"ASM-24\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns an unresolved temperature-history gap affecting stock, along with stock status and budget values\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-22.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned stock status and budget values without presenting an estimated charge to an unobserved tier\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens the affected stock detail\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When the API returns an unresolved temperature-history gap affecting stock, the Meridian responsive web app shall show the returned stock status and budget values without presenting an estimated charge to an unobserved temperature tier.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-22\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"I-13\",\n    \"I-14\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"Q-8\",\n    \"ASM-2\",\n    \"ASM-4\",\n    \"ASM-10\",\n    \"ASM-18\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns a quality-review case linked to a delivered customer order\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-23.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned case status and affected delivered line or stock details\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer or authorized staff user opens the related order or case\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When corrected temperature history identifies an excursion affecting stock already delivered, the Meridian responsive web app shall show the returned quality-review case to the relevant customer and staff users.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-23\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-13\",\n    \"I-14\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A driver has opened today's assigned route while connected and then loses connectivity\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-24.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the route, stops, and delivery details while offline\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver opens the cached route\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A driver records a supported action while offline\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-24.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the action as queued and retains its entered values until synchronization succeeds or the API rejects or refuses the action\",\n     \"when\": \"the action is saved without a connection\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The originating driver signs in again with an enabled account and reconnects\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-24.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned synchronization result for each queued action\",\n     \"when\": \"queued actions synchronize\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A queued action is submitted and the API reports that the originating driver's account is disabled or access is refused\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-24.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned rejection message or error, marks the action as not accepted or synchronized, and shows it as rejected or no longer queued, with no later synchronization request for that action\",\n     \"when\": \"the synchronization response is displayed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Dispatcher changes a cached route or cancels an order while the driver is offline and the API returns the updated route or order on reconnection\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-24.5\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"