r exports the view\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A signed-in user without audit-trail permission opens the audit trail and the service refuses access\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-58.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays an access-denied message and no audit entries, filters, or export action\",\n     \"when\": \"the audit-trail page loads\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide an audit-trail screen showing returned entries with actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason, with filters by record, user, date range, and action type and export of the filtered view.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-58\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"I-13\",\n    \"I-15\",\n    \"I-17\",\n    \"I-18\",\n    \"I-19\",\n    \"I-20\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A lot-history response contains receipt, movement, delivery, or destruction events\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-59.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned events in time order\",\n     \"when\": \"an Auditor opens lot history\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A signed-in user without lot-history permission opens a lot history and the service refuses access\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-59.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays an access-denied message and no lot-history events\",\n     \"when\": \"the lot-history page loads\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show the returned history of a lot from receipt through delivery or destruction in time order.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-59\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The service returns report figures for a selected date range and warehouse\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-60.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays returned excursion counts and rates by route, driver, vehicle, and shipper box type; packs rejected and destroyed by product and cause; on-time delivery and in-full percentages; average time from excursion to decision; stock within 60 days of expiry by product and warehouse; and open recalls and their progress\",\n     \"when\": \"staff open the reports screen\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A staff user has warehouse access scope\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-60.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen offers only in-scope warehouses and the downloaded CSV file contains the displayed filtered figures\",\n     \"when\": \"the user filters reports and exports them\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A signed-in user without report access opens the reports page and the service refuses access\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-60.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays an access-denied message and no report figures or export action\",\n     \"when\": \"the page loads\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide on-screen reports for selected date ranges and warehouses, with CSV export of displayed figures, including excursion counts and rates by route, driver, vehicle, and shipper box type; packs rejected and destroyed by product and cause; deliveries on time within 60 minutes of planned arrival and in full when every ordered pack is handed over, each as a percentage; average time from excursion to decision; stock within 60 days of expiry by product and warehouse; and open recalls and their progress.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-60\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-2\",\n    \"ASM-15\",\n    \"I-50\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An authorized staff user opens opening-inventory entry\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-61.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request contains the entered opening lot and stock fields and the screen displays the returned result or error\",\n     \"when\": \"the user enters lot and stock details\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A signed-in user without opening-inventory permission opens opening-inventory entry and the service refuses access\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-61.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays an access-denied message and no opening-inventory form or records\",\n     \"when\": \"the page loads\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide forms to enter opening lots and stock records and submit them to the service.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-61\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-20\",\n    \"Q-5\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A delivery record within its retention period includes signature and photo evidence\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-62.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the signature and photo fields or their available file links\",\n     \"when\": \"an authorized user opens the delivery record\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A signed-in user without delivery-evidence permission opens a delivery record and the service refuses access\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-62.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays an access-denied message and no signature, photo, or evidence file links\",\n     \"when\": \"the evidence view loads\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall make recorded handover signatures and delivery photos available from a delivery record within its seven-year evidence-retention period.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-62\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  }\n ],\n \"roundTrip\": {\n  \"droppedSpans\": [],\n  \"inventedCapabilities\": []\n },\n \"settled\": [\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"The system shall be sized for 5,000 devices reporting at once.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox, and support the stated first-year user and record volume and simultaneous device volume.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m1 Q-13\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The 28 requirements are estimated at about four runs of work. How would you like the scope handled? → Split the full scope across about four runs; keep all requirements.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"lint\",\n   \"problem\": \"L9 size: This spec has 28 requirements, about 4 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m1 Q-9\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"What should happen to unsynchronized driver actions when a driver signs out or the API reports the account disabled, especially if another user later signs in on the same browser? → Retain unsynchronized actions in a queue tied to the originating driver; sync only after that same driver signs in again, and erase or reject the queue if access is refused or the account is disabled.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"AC-24.8 keeps queued actions, which contain recipient names, after sign-out or a disabled account and later tries to sync them, contradicting REQ-3's rule to clear protected data when access is refused and ASM-17's rule that a disabled driver's queued actions are not accepted.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m1 Q-10\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"What should happen to unsynchronized driver actions when a driver signs out or the API reports the account disabled, especially if another user later signs in on the same browser? → Retain unsynchronized actions in a queue tied to the originating driver; sync only after that same driver signs in again, and erase or reject the queue if access is refused or the account is disabled.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"After a driver signs out with actions still queued, nothing says whose identity the later sync runs under or stops a different user on the same browser from submitting the first driver's queued handovers.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m1 Q-10\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"When a temperature-history gap affects stock, should the stock be automatically placed On Hold while the gap is unresolved, or should the gap be flagged for review without automatically changing stock status? → Flag the gap for review and show the API-returned stock status; do not automatically place the stock On Hold.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"ASM-2 (flag the gap for review without automatically placing stock On Hold) and ASM-18 (keep affected stock On Hold until resolved) directly conflict, and REQ-21 defers to 'the stock status returned by the API' instead of settling which rule applies.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m1 Q-11\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"May a temperature-profile version have an effective date in the past, and if so, how should recalculated results affect stock that was already released or had a quality decision? → Require effective dates to be today or later; do not recalculate earlier decisions.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"AC-6.2 and AC-6.4 allow backdated profile versions that recalculate earlier decisions, but Q-8 never approved backdating, and nothing says what happens to stock already released or already approved by quality that now fails the recalculated budget.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m1 Q-12\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"If an offline handover is queued and the API returns a restriction because the stock went On Hold or was recalled, how should the app handle that recorded handover? → Do not mark the delivery as completed; show the returned restriction and leave the affected quantity outstanding for follow-up.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"Handovers recorded offline are queued and synced later, but AC-16.5 and AC-6.4 rely on a returned 'handover restriction' for stock that went On Hold or was recalled, so an offline driver can hand over held or recalled stock and nothing says what happens to that handover when it syncs.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m1 Q-14\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Q-10 settles that queued actions stay tied to the originating driver across sign-out and workday end, and are erased or rejected if access is refused or the account is disabled. Should any additional local protection or expiry rule apply to queued actions containing recipient names on a shared browser? → Keep the existing same-driver access rule and retain queued actions until sync or API rejection/refusal; add no local encryption or expiry.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"The ears says cached route and delivery data are cleared at sign-out, workday end or refused access, yet unsynced queued actions, which hold recipient names (PII), are kept on a possibly shared browser with no limit on how long they stay or how they are protected.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m1 Q-15\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk\",\n   \"how\": \"open-risk\",\n   \"kind\": \"lint\",\n   \"problem\": \"L6 scope: out-of-scope list is empty; say explicitly what isn't changing\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk\",\n   \"how\": \"open-risk\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"REQ-21 lists ASM-18 as a source, which keeps gap-affected stock On Hold until resolved, but the same requirement (per Q-11/ASM-2) says the screen must not infer On Hold from a gap; the sources contradict each other and nothing settles which wins.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk\",\n   \"how\": \"open-risk\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"REQ-24 and REQ-3 cite ASM-1 and ASM-17 ('No; online only'), yet REQ-24 queues offline driver actions and later syncs them under Q-10, so the sources state opposite rules for queued actions.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk\",\n   \"how\": \"open-risk\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"AC-6.1 and AC-6.3 show API-recalculated 'decision values' after a profile change, but no criterion requires that a changed not-permitted-range disposition goes back through the Quality Officer proposal and different-Quality-Manager approval required by Q-1/REQ-9.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"The driver sees today's route with its stops in order.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Show drivers only their assigned routes for today, with each route’s stops in route order.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-17\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"Loading requires every box on the route to be scanned, and a wrong or missing box is reported.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Compare scanned shipper boxes with expected boxes before departure, report missing or wrong-route boxes, and block departure until every expected box is scanned and wrong boxes are removed or corrected.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-18\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"The dispatcher sees each stop's status and the time it was last updated.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Show dispatchers each route stop’s status and last-updated time.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-19\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"During the route the application shows the current temperature and status of each box and any alerts.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Show each route box’s latest available temperature, status, and gateway alerts, and mark cached temperature data as stale while disconnected.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-20\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"If a box holds stock that is On Hold, the application shows \\\"Do not deliver\\\" for that box and does not allow it to be handed over.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"For scanned boxes on hold, display “Do not deliver” and the returned hold reason, and prevent handover of those boxes.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-21\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"For the remaining boxes, the driver records the receiver's name, captures their signature and a photo of the delivered boxes, and completes the handover. The time and location are recorded automatically.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Let drivers record eligible handovers with receiver name, signature, delivery photo, actual handover time, and available browser location.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-22\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"If the route was changed while the driver was offline, the driver is shown the difference before continuing, and a handover already completed offline is never lost or undone.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"When an assigned route changes while a driver is offline, show route differences, require review and resolution of affected unsent work before continuing, and preserve completed offline handovers.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-23\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"The system shows the reviewer the full temperature history, the budget used and remaining per tier, and a recommendation: Release when every tier still has allowance left, Reject when any tier is used up or a not-permitted range was reached.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Present a single-person quality-decision flow only when an excursion is within the first tier above or below the permitted band, allowance remains, and the proposed decision matches the recommendation. Otherwise require a Quality Officer proposal and separate approval by a different Quality Manager. Require written justification when a decision opposes the recommendation.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-24\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"Each decision is signed electronically: the person confirms their identity again at the moment of signing and gives a reason. A signed decision cannot be edited. It can only be superseded by a new signed decision, and both remain on record.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Require identity confirmation using the account’s sign-in method and a reason when a user signs a quality decision; present signed decisions as read-only with a separate superseding-decision action.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-25\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"If the excursion stayed within the first tier above or below the band and allowance remains, a Quality Officer may decide alone.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"When the service returns a quality disposition, show resulting stock, order, and route status and, when superseded, the earlier and current disposition.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-26\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"Destruction is recorded with a date, a quantity and a witness.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Collect destruction date, quantity, and witness for rejected stock, and prevent entry of a quantity greater than the displayed rejected quantity.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-27\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"Decisions waiting longer than 4 hours are escalated to the Quality Manager.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Identify decisions waiting more than four hours as escalated in the Quality Manager’s waiting-decisions view.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-28\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"A Quality Manager starts a recall for a product and one or more lot numbers, with a reason and a severity.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Provide a Quality Manager flow to start and close recalls with signed actions; recall start collects product, one or more lots, reason, and severity, and the app displays each returned action result.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-29\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"The trace from lot to every location and customer shall be available within one minute of the request.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Display the returned recall trace, including warehouse locations, boxes, routes, customer deliveries, quantities, delivery dates, receivers, and the trace total alongside received quantity when supplied.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-30\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"Notifies those customers by email and in the customer portal.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Show customer recall notices in the portal, link notices to affected deliveries, and provide a response entry point.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-31\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"The customer portal shows the organisation's orders, their status, the lots and expiry dates allocated, and for deliveries on the road the planned arrival time and whether the temperature is in range.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Show customers only their organisation’s current and past orders, allocated lots and expiry dates, order status, and in-transit delivery arrival and temperature status, without exposing other route customers.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-32\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"After delivery, the customer can download a delivery certificate as a PDF for each delivery.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Provide a PDF certificate for each completed delivery in the signed-in customer’s organisation, containing products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver, handover time, each box’s temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions, and signed excursion decisions.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-33\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"Each affected customer responds in the portal with, for each delivery, how many packs are still on hand, how many were used or dispensed, and how many were destroyed on site.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"When late readings produce a new certificate version, list the new and earlier versions for the signed-in customer’s completed delivery and keep each available for download.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-34\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"Recall progress shows the percentage of packs accounted for.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Present the customer portal and certificates in the user’s selected English or Arabic, render Arabic right to left including tables and charts, and show dates and times in the account’s configured time zone.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-35\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"A customer sees current and past orders of their own organisation only.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Provide an audit-trail screen showing returned entries with actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason; support filters by record, user, date range, and action type, and export the filtered view.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-36\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"The certificate contains the contents by lot, the handover details, the temperature chart, and any excursions with their decisions.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Show the returned history of a lot from receipt through delivery or destruction in time order.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-37\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"The same figures shall be available on screen for any date range, filterable by warehouse.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Provide on-screen reports for selected date ranges and warehouses, with CSV export of displayed figures, covering excursion counts and rates by route, driver, vehicle, and shipper box type; packs rejected and destroyed by product and cause; on-time deliveries within 60 minutes of planned arrival and in-full deliveries when every ordered pack is handed over, each as a percentage; average time from excursion to decision; stock within 60 days of expiry by product and warehouse; and open recalls and their progress.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-38\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"The portal and the certificate are available in English and Arabic according to the user's preference.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Make the web app responsive on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-39\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"The request asks for it: \\\"The trace lists every warehouse location, box, route and customer delivery for the lot, with quantities.\\\"\",\n   \"how\": \"in-request\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Render the full recall trace returned by the service for the assumed launch scale.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Should this 34-requirement scope be approved as one run, split into multiple runs, or reduced? → Split the work into about three runs without cutting requirements.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"lint\",\n   \"problem\": \"L9 size: This spec has 34 requirements, about 3 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-9\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"If a driver's session expires while the browser is offline, may the driver continue recording loading, handover, and refusal work? → Allow local recording after expiry, but require the driver to re-authenticate before queued work can sync.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"REQ-12 retains work across session expiry but requires re-authentication before sync, and nothing says whether a driver whose session expires while offline can keep recording work, given that password checks need the service.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-10\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Should recall blocking and conflict handling extend to offline cached recall information, or apply only once the service is reachable? The request separately requires retaining and flagging an offline handover that conflicts with a hold. → Apply recall blocks from the service while online; do not add offline-cache recall blocking or a separate recall-conflict quality-case flow.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"When a scanned box is recalled according to the service or offline cache, display “Do not deliver” and prevent its handover.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-11\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Should recall blocking and conflict handling extend to offline cached recall information, or apply only once the service is reachable? The request separately requires retaining and flagging an offline handover that conflicts with a hold. → Apply recall blocks from the service while online; do not add offline-cache recall blocking or a separate recall-conflict quality-case flow.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"When an offline handover conflicts with a hold or recall during synchronization, retain and flag the handover and display the returned quality-case result.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-11\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"If the browser denies or cannot provide location, should an otherwise eligible handover still be allowed? → Allow the handover and record the location as unavailable.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Allow otherwise eligible handovers when browser location is denied or unavailable, and record location as unavailable.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-12\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Should the offline queue include safeguards beyond the requested local work retention and automatic sending, such as account isolation, re-authentication, retry identifiers, and review of permanently rejected payloads? → Keep the requested offline queue and automatic sending, without adding the extra account-isolation and rejected-payload review rules.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"While offline, retain loading, handover, and refusal work locally across session expiry or sign-out; isolate queued work to its originating account; require that user to re-authenticate before syncing; automatically send queued work when connectivity returns; preserve handover occurrence time and identifier on retries; clear payloads only after successful acknowledgement; and retain permanently rejected payloads for user review before retry. If local storage cannot retain a complete payload, show an error and do not report the work as queued.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-13\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Should the web app have a formal browser support requirement for the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox? → Do not add a fixed browser-version support requirement.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Support the latest two browser versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-14\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Should WCAG 2.1 AA conformance be added as an acceptance requirement for the main flows? → Do not add a formal WCAG 2.1 AA requirement.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Conform the main web-app flows to WCAG 2.1 AA.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-15\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Should a first-year product scale target be defined in this scope, in addition to the requested one-minute lot-trace availability? → Do not add a first-year product scale target; retain the explicitly requested lot-trace timing.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Support the assumed first-year product scale and make a requested lot trace available through its screen within the requested time limit.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-16\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"How should the web app complete password reset after a user opens the reset link, including when the link is invalid or expired? → Open a form to set a new password; for an invalid or expired link, explain that it cannot be used and let the user request another reset email.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"AC-1.2 covers only requesting a reset email; there is no screen or criterion for opening the reset link and setting a new password, or for an expired or invalid link, so self-service reset can't be completed or tested.\",\n   \"ref\": \"m2 Q-41\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk\",\n   \"how\": \"open-risk\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"AC-16.1 picks the single-person controls when an eligible Quality Officer 'opens the decision form' based on whether 'the proposed decision matches the recommendation', but the decision is not proposed until the officer is inside that form, which clashes with AC-16.4 ('when a user prepares the decision').\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk\",\n   \"how\": \"open-risk\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"There is no path for a Quality Manager declining or returning a Quality Officer's proposal, and no state for a declined proposal, so a two-person decision can only end in approval.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk\",\n   \"how\": \"open-risk\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"AC-17.1 requires identity confirmation at signing but has no criterion for a failed confirmation (wrong password) or an expired session, for example that nothing is shown as signed and the reason entered is kept.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk\",\n   \"how\": \"open-risk\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"Handover has no validation path for a missing receiver name, signature or photo, and none for camera permission being denied or the photo capture failing.\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"cb\" kind=\"current-behaviour\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"claims\": [],\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-12T19:22:21.911Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"current-behaviour\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"stage\": \"ground\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261012-meridian-coldchain-platform-in-9fcb\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"notFound\": [\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-1\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-2\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-3\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-4\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\